📌 1️⃣ Requirement Gathering / Business Requirement

👉 Understanding what the client wants

What problem to solve?

What KPIs are needed?

Who will use the dashboard?

🧠 Example:
Hospital wants to track waiting time, patient count, satisfaction.

📌 2️⃣ Data Walkthrough

👉 Understanding the data structure

What columns are there?

Meaning of each column

Data type (date, number, text)

🧠 Example:
Patient ID, Arrival Time, Gender, Department, etc.

📌 3️⃣ Data Connection

👉 Connecting Power BI to data source

Excel

CSV

Database

SQL Server

🧠 Example:
Connecting ER patient CSV file to Power BI.

📌 4️⃣ Data Cleaning / Quality Check

👉 Fixing wrong or missing data

Remove duplicates

Handle missing values

Correct formats

🧠 Example:
Fix wrong dates, remove empty patient IDs.

📌 5️⃣ Data Modeling

👉 Creating relationships between tables

One-to-many relations

Primary & foreign keys

🧠 Example:
Link Patient table with Date table.

📌 6️⃣ Data Processing

👉 Transforming data for analysis

Create new columns

Group data

Filter data

🧠 Example:
Create Age Group from Age.

📌 7️⃣ DAX Calculations

👉 Writing formulas to calculate KPIs

Measures

Calculated columns

🧠 Example:
Average Wait Time, % Seen within 30 mins.

📌 8️⃣ Dashboard Layouting

👉 Designing dashboard structure

Where charts go

Card positions

Filters placement

🧠 Example:
KPIs on top, charts below.

📌 9️⃣ Charts Development & Formatting

👉 Creating and styling charts

Bar, pie, line charts

Colors, labels, fonts

🧠 Example:
Bar chart for patients by day.

📌 🔟 Dashboard / Report Development

👉 Building the final interactive dashboard

Slicers

Tooltips

Navigation buttons

🧠 Example:
Monthly view & consolidated view pages.

📌 1️⃣1️⃣ Insights Generation

👉 Finding meaningful conclusions from data

Trends

Problems

Improvements

🧠 Example:
Waiting time is higher on Thursdays.
